In article <979@eutrc3.urc.tue.nl> wsinrn@eutrc3.urc.tue.nl (r.nauta) writes:

>Before you can cast a spell,
>you must transcribe it, that means memorize a spellbook. you do that with
>the 'X'. That destroys the spellbook, but makes you able to cast the spell
>with 'Z'. Early on you might miss the strength to do so, but later on it's
>easy...

This is how spells work up to 2.3

In Nethack 3.0 the spellbooks are read with the "r" command, just like
a scroll is.  To cast a spell use the "Z" command.  To get an inventory of your
memorized spells, use the "x" command. 

Casting a spell requires Power.  The amount of Power a spell requires is shown in your
spell inventory, ie

polymorph (6)

This means that you can cast polymorph and it costs you six Power points every time.
It does NOT mean that you can necessarily cast six polymorphs.

